// Where does generated function number N live?
//
// `id` allows 3 functions per file and 3 entries per directory, so a project
// is a ternary tree: 3 functions to a file, 3 files to a leaf directory
// (9 functions), and every level above multiplies by 3 again. This computes a
// path from a function number with no bookkeeping at all, which is what lets
// the emitter stay stateless -- it can emit function 4,000 without knowing
// anything about functions 0 through 3,999.
//
// Function N is in file N/3. File F is in leaf directory F/3. Leaf directory
// D is reached by writing D in base 3, most significant digit first, and
// taking one directory level per digit. DEPTH fixes how many levels there
// are, so every leaf sits at the same depth and no directory ever mixes files
// with subdirectories -- which would otherwise blow the 3-entry limit.

// 3^5 = 243 leaf directories = 2187 functions. A translated kernel file needs
// far fewer; a whole subsystem may need one more level, and this is the only
// number to change.
tree_depth() {
} return int 5;

funcs_per_file() {
} return int 3;

// Digit `d` (0 = most significant) of `n` written in base 3, padded to
// tree_depth() digits.
tri_digit(int n, int d) {
  int shift = tree_depth() - 1 - d;
  int div = pow3(shift);
  int r = (n / div) % 3;
} return int r;
